ay morning. It will then fall below flood stage Thursday\nmorning.\n- Flood stage is 23.0 feet.\n\n- Http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMexican Hat, Bluff, Montezuma Creek, and Aneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-05T17:15:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.00b8de8d3d582a70415755093091fe5b78bb2bcf.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.00b8de8d3d582a70415755093091fe5b78bb2bcf.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 1 at 10:50AM MST until November 2 at 7:00PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Grand Junction CO has issued a\nFlood Warning for the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nMancos River near Mancos affecting Montezuma County.\n\nFor the Mancos River...including Mancos...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Mancos River near Mancos.\n\n* WHEN...From this evening to Monday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 6.0 feet, Minor flooding can be expected around\nMancos.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 10:00 AM MST Sunday the stage was 4.8 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage this\nevening to a crest of 6.3 feet late this evening. It will then\nfall below flood stage late tonight.\n- Flood stage is 6.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 5.7\nfeet on 05/21/2005.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T19:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0807a2df4e98bab16c60e02a74ad5937530b2c74.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0807a2df4e98bab16c60e02a74ad5937530b2c74.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-02T23:47:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 022347 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discuss